\title{The Algebraic and Coding-Theoretic Toolkit}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    The mathematics the protocols are built out of. Most of the recent performance work lives here rather than in the protocol layer: the same FRI-shaped argument became an order of magnitude faster because the field changed, not because the argument did.
}

\p{
    This is also the part of the stack [CompPoly](dhsorens-0041) is about — fields, polynomials, and their computable representations — so these pages should stay close to what is actually definable in [Lean](dhsorens-lean).
}

